// The project manifest for the native Cadenza agent HARNESS — the agent loop authored IN Cadenza,
// the piece that replaces the headless `claude` CLI (see implementation/design/DESIGN-agent-harness.md).
// `cdz` reads these well-known top-level defs to build/run/test the project (a def is the manifest).
//
//   cdz test          — search up for this Project.cdz and run its suite (like cargo)
//   cdz test .        — same, naming this directory
//
// This is Increment 2: the LOOP SPINE, authored + gated in Cadenza, with a MOCK model/tools handled
// in-program. The model call (`Model.converse : String -> String`) and tool dispatch (`Tools.*`) are
// EFFECTS; an in-program `handle … with` supplies the mock (the free test-override — a nearer handler
// wins over an outer/peer binding), so the SAME loop swaps to a real `cadenza:bedrock/api` peer +
// hive-inbox peer with no code change once those peer shims land (Increment 1b).

def name = "agent-harness"

// Every source module under src/ (a wildcard — a new loop stage just drops into src/).
def modules = ["src/*.cdz"]

// The modules whose `@test` definitions form the suite (same-file with their code for now).
def tests = ["src/*.cdz"]

// Files removed from the globs above. Empty — every src/*.cdz is both a module and its own tests.
def exclude = []
